WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.760
It's Tuesday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your day in Microsoft updates, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.490
Look before you leap.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.380
Manchester's students will get Microsoft 365 Copilot, after a pilot.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.490
Selected programmes try it next semester; every student follows in 2027/28.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.480
Why wait?

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.390
Students and academics asked for clear guidance on AI in learning and assessment first.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.880
Meanwhile, every Manchester student can already use Copilot Chat,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.640
and their prompts aren't used to train the models.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.860
Making handouts?

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.840
Word's Accessibility Assistant now flags bold text that only looks like a heading, for Insiders.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.910
Real headings let screen reader users jump straight to each section.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.420
Running student portals on Power Pages?

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.340
Admins can now allow or block each sign-in method, in preview.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.290
Block Google,

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.500
Facebook or local passwords per site; anyone still using a blocked one can't sign in.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.580
Still running file servers?

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.300
Azure now walks you through syncing Arc-enabled ones to Azure Files, in preview.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.720
Cloud tiering keeps busy files on the se

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.000
rver and moves rarely used ones to Azure.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.940
In calmer news,

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.180
Microsoft tested AI coding agents with the same code but different version numbers.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.680
Labelled a patch,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:44.080
one model checked a breaking upgrade in 2 of 10 runs; labelled major, all 10.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.090
The fine print? From January,

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:52.060
new Fabric workspaces get one SQL pool that can use all the compute.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.050
Outlook.com bouncing school emails?

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:59.340
Microsoft's reportedly investigating; check SPF and DMARC.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.710
After hours? Holiday shopping?

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.940
Edge now offers to compare similar products you've got open in tabs.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.410
In US English, it'll also look for a working coupon at checkout.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.080
On Xbox and PC,

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.860
FragPunk's Farlands is in early access: deliver cargo through a changing world.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.500
Pilot it first, check your headings,

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.060
compare before you buy: look before you leap.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.620
Some of it's shipped. The rest is on its way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
